1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,400
My brother Jack was so smart that he earned a full scholarship to Harvard.
我哥哥杰克非常聪明，拿到了哈佛的全额奖学金。

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:13,420
I often wished he wasn’t so perfect because it made me feel like I had to work twice as hard just to prove myself to others.
我常常希望他不要那么完美，因为他让我觉得，我得付出加倍的努力，才能向别人证明自己。

3
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:22,180
On one hand, his success was a challenge that I enjoyed, but on the other hand, it was an immense pressure that I struggled to cope with.
一方面，他的成功是一种我乐于接受的挑战；另一方面，这也是一种我难以应对的巨大压力。

4
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:30,350
To match his record in high school, I felt like I was constantly running on a treadmill, dedicating every moment to a non-stop race.
为了赶上他高中时的成绩，我觉得自己仿佛一直在跑步机上奔跑，把每一刻都投入到一场永不停歇的赛跑中。

5
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:35,060
There was no room for relaxation as I pursued that perfect record.
为了追求那份完美的成绩，我根本没有放松的余地。

6
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:40,240
My life seemed to be compressed into a series of endless tasks and deadlines.
我的生活似乎被压缩成了一连串没完没了的任务和截止期限。

7
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:49,210
“I need an A,” I repeated to myself before the biology test, so that I would maintain my perfect record and secure a place on the honor roll.
生物考试前，我一遍遍对自己说：“我必须拿A。”这样才能保住我的完美成绩，稳稳登上光荣榜。

8
00:00:50,010 --> 00:00:53,130
I studied till the last minute of lunch and rushed to class.
我一直学到午饭时间的最后一分钟，然后匆匆赶去上课。

9
00:00:53,930 --> 00:01:00,360
I felt a sense of confidence as I glanced over the first page of the test, quickly filling in the answers with a smile.
我扫了一眼试卷的第一页，觉得很有把握，便面带微笑，飞快地填起答案来。

10
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:04,730
However, as I turned to the last page, my mind went blank.
然而，翻到最后一页时，我的脑子一下子一片空白。

11
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:12,350
Time ticked by, and soon, the classroom began to empty as the other students finished their tests and left.
时间一分一秒地过去，很快，其他同学陆续答完试卷离开，教室里渐渐空了。

12
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:14,530
“Lara, class is over.
“劳拉，下课了。

13
00:01:15,330 --> 00:01:19,680
I need you to hand in your test,” Mrs. Phloem said, stretching out her hand.
你得交卷了。”弗洛姆老师说着，伸出了手。

14
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,800
Reluctantly, I handed her the test paper.
我不情愿地把试卷递给了她。

15
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:26,240
The next day, I received my test back.
第二天，试卷发回来了。

16
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:30,290
I stared dumbfounded at the red mark: 76.
我目瞪口呆地盯着那个红色的分数：76。

17
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:33,740
Not even a B minus, my mind screamed.
连B减都不到，我在心里尖叫着。

18
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:35,520
Just average.
只是中等水平。

19
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:37,110
It’s over.
全完了。

20
00:01:37,910 --> 00:01:39,120
No perfect record.
完美成绩没了。

21
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:43,680
I felt an unprecedented sense of frustration and disappointment.
我感到一种前所未有的沮丧和失望。

22
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,480
After school, I dragged my heavy feet back home.
放学后，我拖着沉重的脚步回到家。

23
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:52,310
When I pushed open the door, Jack was sitting on the couch, reading.
我推开门时，杰克正坐在沙发上看书。

24
00:01:53,110 --> 00:01:59,000
Seeing his leisurely state, I cried, unable to contain the jealousy and sadness in my heart.
看到他那副悠闲的样子，我再也忍不住心中的嫉妒和难过，哭了起来。

25
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:02,320
Jack immediately noticed the depression on my face.
杰克立刻注意到了我脸上的沮丧。

26
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:06,440
He asked with concern, “What’s wrong, Lara?”
他关切地问：“怎么了，劳拉？”

27
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:13,620
Blinded by frustration mixed with a touch of jealousy, I shouted at him, “How I wish you were not so perfect!”
沮丧中夹杂着一丝嫉妒，冲昏了我的头脑，我冲他喊道：“我真希望你没那么完美！”

28
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:18,390
With a hint of hurt and surprise in his eyes, Jack gently approached me.
杰克眼中带着一丝受伤和惊讶，温和地走近我。

29
00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:24,100
His words were like a warm breeze, blowing my depression away and changing my mindset.
他的话就像一阵暖风，吹散了我的沮丧，也改变了我的心态。
